Path B bypass: classic WDTT vs RAW (qWDTT / SpaceNeuroX)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

**Classic WDTT** (amurcanov) is **WireGuard over TURN/DTLS** — not the Path B
mode used by ARDTT:

  https://github.com/amurcanov/proxy-turn-vk-android

**RAW Path B** (`-listen-raw`, `raw.go`, RAWCONF / GETCONF_RAW, no nested
WireGuard, no DTLS on that listener) comes from the **qWDTT / SpaceNeuroX**
lineage (fork/continuation of the WDTT idea), GPL-3.0:

  https://github.com/SpaceNeuroX/proxy-turn-vk-android

Vendored server sources under `server/bypass/wdtt-server/` (built as
`wdtt-server -listen-raw`) and the Android Path B client under `android/go_client/`
(`libclient.so` via `scripts/build-bypass-client.sh`) follow that RAW-capable
tree. The RAW TUN uses ARDTT `10.9.0.0/24` (gateway `10.9.0.1`). A small client
patch allows `-n` workers of 1–9 without forcing multiples of 9.

Directory names may still say `wdtt-*` for historical/vendor reasons; the
**product** name is ARDTT (Amnezia + RAW Dial via TURN), not WDTT.

